# Backend Rules

- Use type hints and Pydantic models at external boundaries.
- Keep routers thin; put business logic in explicit service modules.
- Use async only where the underlying I/O library supports it; do not mix sync and async carelessly.
- Use SQLAlchemy and Alembic migrations; no ad-hoc production schema changes.
- Enforce tenant scoping in repository/service methods and, where suitable, PostgreSQL row-level security as defense in depth.
- Never let LLM-generated SQL execute against production data.
- Represent workflow state with explicit typed schemas and durable checkpoints.
- External tool calls require a policy decision and idempotency strategy.
- Use structured errors, trace IDs and redacted logs. Do not log secrets, raw credentials or unnecessary PII.
- Write unit and integration tests for authorization, state transitions and failure cases.
